Heat transfer modeling for supercritical methane flowing in rocket engine cooling channels
Marco Pizzarelli a, *, Francesco Nasuti a, Marcello Onofri a, Pietro Roncioni b, Raffaele Votta b, Francesco Battista b
a University of Rome “La Sapienza”, Dipartimento di Ingegneria Meccanica e Aerospaziale, Via Eudossiana 18, 00184 Rome, Italy b CIRA (Italian Aerospace Research Center), Via Maiorise, 81043 Capua, CE, Italy
highlights
Numerical simulation of methane in supercritical pressure and subcritical to supercritical temperature. Fluid and structure thermal coupling. Asymmetrically heated channels of rectangular cross section. Supercritical-pressure methane may exhibit heat transfer deterioration. Heat transfer deterioration is mitigated increasing coolant pressure and/or surface roughness.
